# Nothing under data/ is committed except the provenance manifest.
#
# Raw downloads are large and reproducible via `python -m data_prep.download`.
# interim/ and processed/ are derived from them -- and because the Nesta
# suitability data is CC BY-NC-SA, committing those derivatives would impose a
# non-commercial share-alike licence on the repository. Worth an explicit
# decision before any of it is checked in.
#
# MANIFEST.md IS committed: it records the URL, licence, retrieval date and
# SHA256 of every snapshot, which is what makes a past result reproducible once
# the upstream files move (Nesta are retiring the suitability dataset).
raw/*
!raw/MANIFEST.md
interim/
processed/
